WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.748 --> 00:00:08.424
This page is where the whole course comes together without flattening it. One world does not mean one answer.

2
00:00:08.424 --> 00:00:18.814
Work the Living World Atlas tabs. Each numbered tab is one move in the synthesis. Read the panel and answer its prompt in your own head before moving on.

3
00:00:18.814 --> 00:00:29.827
Check your current route panel. It shows your program lens and learning emphasis working together on the course's final questions. Change either from the home page; the required curriculum stays identical on every route.

4
00:00:29.827 --> 00:00:40.713
Look at the contexts in your orbit. Contexts you selected in the Cultural Comparison Lab appear here, still distinct. The globe never merges them into one story.

5
00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:51.716
Write your synthesis trail. Four private prompts: one question worth carrying, one source and its job, one difference that must remain, and what follows for you. Each asks for a decision the site cannot make for you.

6
00:00:51.716 --> 00:01:02.721
Treat this as preparation, not assessment prose. The official assessment instructions and grading stay on Blackboard. Use these notes to remember your reasoning, then build your own submission from the assigned sources.

7
00:01:02.721 --> 00:01:08.409
Nothing here is scored or submitted. Blackboard is the only official channel.

8
00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:13.836
Where next: Open Week 14 and carry your trail into the final week's work.
